Z||000005||lharvey71||10-04-2001||01:20 AM||||after all that the switch is not the solution to my problem. the dashboard lights still do not come on. when i turn the wheel dial all the way to the top the interior lights come on, as they did with the old switch. im at a total loss on what it could be. again ive checked and rechecked the fuses, also i checked the bulbs and all fifteen of them are in working order. is there a relay or something that im not aware of that could be faulty? someone with any advice please!!||||reg||9
Z||000006||Wolfhound||10-04-2001||06:44 AM||||Pull the connections on the back of the instrument cluster and check for corrosion.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Banzai||10-04-2001||07:05 AM||||could be a broken circuit on the board. Take the cluster out and look it over well. Can be fixed with a kit from Radio Shack.<P>Banzai !!!!!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000008||Rodney||10-04-2001||08:24 AM||||I'm guessing it is the dimmer transistor under the dash. The connections get corroded and the dash lights do not light up. Find and take it out and make sure all the legs on the transistor make good contact to the clips that hold them in. I'm sure there is a way to just bypass it so the lights stay full bright also. This transistor is mounted on an aluminum heat sink plate.||||reg||1
